# cPanel MCP — prod read-only

The **`cpanel-acso`** MCP server uses one cPanel account (`CPANEL_USER`). UAPI does not auto-scope to staging — **the agent must enforce scope**.

## Production (`samoorg.com.ua`, prod `public_html`, prod DB, prod DNS zone for main domain)

**Only read-only MCP tools** — inventory and inspection:

- Allowed patterns: `list`, `get`, `read`, `fetch`, `status`, `stats`, `bandwidth` (read), view configs without save.
- Examples: list files under prod paths (read-only), get PHP version, list MySQL databases/users (no create/delete), get DNS records, list SSL certs, list cron (do not add/remove).

**Never on production scope** (refuse even if user asks in chat):
        
- Any tool that **creates, updates, deletes, saves, installs, sets, adds, removes, modifies, deploys, restores, or writes** files/DB/DNS/SSL/email/cron/domains/PHP.
- File Manager **save**, **delete**, **chmod**, **move** on prod paths.
- MySQL **create** / **delete** / **set_privileges** for prod databases.
- DNS **add** / **delete** / **edit** for `samoorg.com.ua`.
- **PHP set version** on shared hosting (one PHP per account — see migration rules); do not change without explicit cutover plan + backup.

If a tool might affect prod and scope is unclear → **do not call it**; ask user or use SSH read-only listing instead.

## Staging (`staging.samoorg.com.ua`, `STAGING_DOCROOT` in `secrets/acso.env`)

- **Writes allowed** only for staging subdomain, staging docroot, and **new staging DB** (not prod DB names).
- Before mutating: confirm path/domain is staging, not `public_html` prod root.

## Shared hosting (Hostpro, skm352)

- **One PHP version per cPanel user** — applies to all sites on the account until host changes it globally.
- **MySQL/MariaDB** on skm352 is current enough for WordPress 6.x (per host support); create **separate DB** for staging in cPanel.
